  "ai_overview": {
    "text_blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "To file a roof insurance claim in Utah, follow these step-by-step guidelines based on Utah Insurance Department recommendations and local roofing standards:",
        "snippet_links": [
          {
            "text": "Utah Insurance Department",
            "link": "https://insurance.utah.gov/consumers/home-insurance/home-claims-info/"
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "1. Document the Damage First"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Take photos and video: Capture dated, close-up and wide-angle photos of the roof, missing or dented shingles, gutters, screens, and any collateral damage before doing anything else.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              1,
              2
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Get an independent inspection: Call a reputable, licensed local Utah roofing contractor (such as Homer Roofing or Reimagine Roofing ) to perform a free pre-inspection and create a detailed photo report. This helps confirm whether you actually have enough storm damage to justify filing a claim.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              1,
              3
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Avoid \"storm chasers\": Do not sign a contingency agreement or assignment of benefits pushed by door-to-door contractors offering to \"handle everything\" or absorb your deductible.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              1,
              4
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "2. Make Temporary Emergency Repairs"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Prevent further harm: If water is leaking into your home or the roof is exposed, put up a tarp or make temporary emergency fixes to stop additional destruction.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0,
              2
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Save all receipts: Keep every receipt for materials, labor, or emergency supplies. Most policies cover reasonable costs to protect your property from secondary damage.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0,
              2
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "3. Contact Your Insurance Company"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Report the loss promptly: Call your insurance carrier's claims line or log into their online portal as soon as possible. Be ready to provide:",
            "list": [
              {
                "snippet": "The date of loss (when the storm or damage happened)"
              },
              {
                "snippet": "The type of peril (e.g., severe wind, hail, or heavy snow load)"
              },
              {
                "snippet": "A factual, objective description of the damage (avoid admitting to old age or pre-existing wear-and-tear)",
                "reference_indexes": [
                  0,
                  1,
                  3,
                  5,
                  6
                ]
              }
            ],
            "reference_indexes": [
              0,
              1,
              3,
              5,
              6
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Record your claim number: Write down the claim number and the name/phone number of your assigned claims adjuster.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              4,
              5,
              7
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "4. Meet the Adjuster on the Roof"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Have your roofer present: Schedule the insurance adjuster\u2019s visit and make sure your chosen, licensed roofing contractor is physically present on the roof with them.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              1,
              3,
              6
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Ensure a fair evaluation: Your contractor can point out functional storm damage (like bruised shingles, soft decking, or fractured mats) that an insurance adjuster might otherwise overlook.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              6
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "5. Review the Scope of Work and Payout"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Audit the estimate: Once the insurance company issues an itemized scope of work, have your contractor review it to ensure all necessary repair or replacement costs are included.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              3
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Understand the funds: You will typically receive an initial Actual Cash Value (ACV) check (minus your deductible) to start the work, followed by depreciation funds (Replacement Cost Value) once the project is finished.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              3
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you run into disputes or unfair settlement practices with your carrier, you can contact the Utah Insurance Department consumer assistance line at 801-957-9305 or 800-439-3805.",
        "snippet_links": [
          {
            "text": "Utah Insurance Department",
            "link": "https://insurance.utah.gov/consumers/home-insurance/home-claims-info/"
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you'd like to share:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "What type of damage occurred (hail, wind, fallen tree)?"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "When did the storm happen?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "I can give you more specific details on what to watch out for during your adjuster meeting."
      }
    ],
